---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
const faqs = [
  {q:'Are my spreadsheet files uploaded?',a:'No. This converter reads the selected file in your browser. The file contents, file name and JSON output are not sent to our servers or analytics. Copying or downloading the result happens only when you choose it.'},
  {q:'Which Excel formats are supported?',a:'Use .xlsx files or UTF-8 .csv files up to 10 MB. Legacy .xls, password-protected workbooks and macro-enabled .xlsm files are not supported. Save those as .xlsx or UTF-8 CSV in your spreadsheet application first. Each selected sheet may contain up to 10,000 data rows and 200 columns.'},
  {q:'How are headers, empty cells and duplicate names handled?',a:'With First row contains column names selected, each data row becomes an object. Blank headers become Column 1, Column 2 and so on. Duplicate names receive numbered suffixes so no column is overwritten. Empty cells become null; fully empty rows are skipped. Turn off headers to get an array of arrays.'},
  {q:'Are numbers, dates and leading zeros preserved?',a:'CSV values remain strings, preserving identifiers such as 0012. XLSX cells retain their stored numeric, text or boolean type; dates become ISO strings. Excel number formatting, including zeros displayed only by a number format, is not preserved. Formulas are not recalculated; only saved values are read.'}
];
const related = [
  {href:'/everyday/word-counter',icon:'📝',title:'Word Counter',desc:'Inspect text length'},
  {href:'/everyday/case-converter',icon:'Aa',title:'Case Converter',desc:'Change text case'},
  {href:'/construction/material-planner',icon:'📋',title:'Material Planner',desc:'Create and export a shopping list'},
  {href:'/converters/unit-converter',icon:'⇄',title:'Unit Converter',desc:'Convert measurements'}
];
---
<CalculatorLayout title="Excel to JSON Converter: XLSX & CSV, No Upload" h1="Excel to JSON Converter" description="Convert XLSX or CSV to JSON in your browser. Export one worksheet or all sheets, preview the result and download JSON. Files stay on your device. No account or upload." subtitle="Choose a spreadsheet or paste CSV. Preview the JSON, then copy or download it. Your file stays on your device." category="Converters" categoryHref="/converters" appCategory="UtilitiesApplication" faqs={faqs} relatedTools={related} showAds={false}>
  <div slot="calculator" class="xlsx-tool">
    <noscript><p>JavaScript is required to read files locally. No file is uploaded.</p></noscript>
    <div class="field"><label for="xj-file">Choose an XLSX or CSV file</label><input id="xj-file" type="file" accept=".xlsx,.csv" /><p class="hint">Up to 10 MB. Up to 10,000 data rows and 200 columns per sheet. Legacy .xls files must be saved as .xlsx first.</p></div>
    <div class="field" id="xj-sheet-field" hidden><label for="xj-sheet">Worksheet</label><select id="xj-sheet"></select></div>
    <details class="csv-paste"><summary>Or paste CSV text</summary>
      <div class="field"><label for="xj-csv">CSV text (UTF-8)</label><textarea id="xj-csv" rows="5" placeholder={'Code,Quantity\n0012,3'}></textarea></div>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="xj-convert">Convert pasted CSV</button>
    </details>
    <div class="xlsx-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="xj-workbook-sample">Try sample XLSX</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="xj-sample">Try sample CSV</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="xj-clear">Clear</button></div>
    <p class="hint"><a href="/examples/inventory.xlsx" download>Download the sample workbook</a> to test a file from your device. It contains made-up inventory and an empty second sheet.</p>
    <label class="header-option"><input type="checkbox" id="xj-headers" checked /> First row contains column names</label>
    <p id="xj-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Select a file or try the sample to begin.</p>
    <p id="xj-error" role="alert"></p>
    <div id="xj-result" hidden>
      <p id="xj-header-note" class="hint"></p>
      <div class="field"><label for="xj-output">JSON output</label><textarea id="xj-output" readonly rows="14" spellcheck="false"></textarea></div>
      <div class="xlsx-actions"><button type="button" id="xj-copy" class="btn btn-primary">Copy JSON</button><button type="button" id="xj-download" class="btn btn-secondary">Download JSON</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>How to convert XLSX to JSON</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Choose an XLSX file. If it has multiple sheets, select one worksheet or <strong>All worksheets</strong>.</li>
      <li>Keep <strong>First row contains column names</strong> checked to turn rows into objects. Uncheck it for arrays of cells.</li>
      <li>Check the preview, then copy the JSON or download it as a <code>.json</code> file.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>What does the JSON look like?</h2>
    <p>One sheet gives you a JSON array. All worksheets gives you a single object keyed by sheet name, with one array per sheet. An empty sheet becomes <code>[]</code>. The combined export supports up to 10,000 data rows.</p>
    <pre>{'{\n  "Inventory": [{"Code": "0012", "Quantity": 3, "Enabled": true}],\n  "Empty": []\n}'}</pre>
    <p><strong>Preserving ZIP codes or IDs?</strong> Store them as text in Excel before converting. A value stored as the number <code>12</code> and only displayed as <code>0012</code> by cell formatting will export as <code>12</code>.</p>
    <h2>CSV to JSON example</h2>
    <p>A CSV containing <code>Code,Quantity</code> followed by <code>0012,3</code> becomes <code>{'[{"Code":"0012","Quantity":"3"}]'}</code>. CSV cells stay strings, so the leading zeros in an identifier are not silently removed.</p>
    <h2>Check the result before importing it elsewhere</h2>
    <p>Only cell values are converted. Styling, charts, merged-cell layouts and Excel display formats are not preserved. Dates are represented as ISO strings, empty cells as null, and duplicate headers are renamed visibly. Formula cells use their saved values; this tool does not calculate formulas.</p>
    <p>For files using legacy formats or passwords, open them in your spreadsheet application and save an unprotected .xlsx or UTF-8 CSV copy first. Keep identifiers as text in the source workbook when their leading zeros matter. Large or unusually complex workbooks may exceed your browser's memory.</p>
  </section>
</CalculatorLayout>
<script>import '../../scripts/excel-to-json.js';</script>
<style>
  .xlsx-tool textarea {width:100%;resize:vertical;min-height:110px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.6;padding:12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;}
  .xlsx-actions {display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:16px 0;}
  .xlsx-actions button {min-height:44px;}
  .csv-paste {padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}
  .csv-paste summary {cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;}
  .csv-paste .field {margin-top:16px;}
  .header-option {display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px;}
  .header-option input {width:auto;}
  #xj-status {margin:16px 0;color:var(--primary-dark);}
  #xj-error {color:#b91c1c;}
</style>
